S("Start", "What it took", f"""<div class="body" style="margin-top:14px;gap:44px;flex:none"><div style="width:1190px;flex:none"><div style="display:flex;gap:8px;margin-bottom:8px" id="t2-stages"></div><svg id="t2-chart" class="dia" viewBox="0 0 1000 470" style="height:370px;width:100%" preserveAspectRatio="none" role="img" aria-label="Tricky question accuracy during our training"></svg></div>
<div style="flex:1;min-width:0"><div class="kick" style="font-size:19px;margin-bottom:6px">8 real questions &times; their 8 answers</div><div style="width:370px"><div id="t2-mat"></div></div><div class="mono" style="font-size:19px;margin-top:8px" id="t2-hits"></div><p style="margin-top:8px"><button id="t2-go" style="font-size:18px;padding:8px 14px">Replay</button></p></div></div>
<div class="grid4" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr) 1.15fr 1.15fr;gap:20px;margin-top:10px"><div class="tile hot" style="padding-top:10px"><div class="n" style="font-size:18px">Step</div><div style="font-size:42px;font-weight:300;margin-top:6px" id="t2-step">0</div></div><div class="tile hot" style="padding-top:10px"><div class="n" style="font-size:18px">Pairs seen</div><div style="font-size:42px;font-weight:300;margin-top:6px" id="t2-seen">0</div></div><div class="tile hot" style="padding-top:10px"><div class="n" style="font-size:18px">General loss</div><div style="font-size:42px;font-weight:300;margin-top:6px" id="t2-loss">6.93</div></div><div class="tile hot" style="padding-top:10px"><div class="n" style="font-size:18px">Tricky test</div><div style="font-size:42px;font-weight:300;color:#4d6bfe;margin-top:6px" id="t2-acc">8.0%</div></div>{stat("Parameters", "18.9M trained", "on a frozen 8.19B encoder")}{stat("GPUs and cost", "About $137", "1 L40S per training stage")}</div>""", "This replay starts by itself, from our real logs of today: 30,000 pre-training steps, 1,008 mid-training steps and 400 post-training steps. Totals: 63.3M pairs, about 3 hours of training, and about $137 of Modal compute including tests. Embedding the agent data used 8 L40S and 12 H100. Watch the diagonal of the matrix form.", "Our real training run, replayed", "We rebuilt it <i>this afternoon</i>")

S("Start", "Dinosaur", '''<div class="body"><div class="col w3"><video src="media/ours_shield_on_off.mp4" controls muted loop playsinline preload="auto" style="width:100%;max-height:790px;display:block;border:1px solid #dcdcdc"></video></div>
<div class="col"><div class="tile hot"><div class="n">Answer time</div><h3 style="font-size:64px;font-weight:300">17.1 ms</h3></div><div class="tile" style="margin-top:18px"><div class="n">Decisions per 60 s</div><h3 style="font-size:64px;font-weight:300">3,268</h3></div><div class="tile" style="margin-top:18px"><div class="n">Courses survived, shield on</div><h3 style="font-size:64px;font-weight:300">3 of 5</h3></div><p class="note" style="margin-top:16px">Real recorded frames of our model, with our own simple graphics. Top: shield on. Bottom: shield off.</p></div></div>''', "Top lane shield on, bottom lane shield off. Same head, same course. Be open that the shield does a lot of work.", "Video: our model", "Our model plays <i>at 60 frames per second</i>")

S("Start", "Answering", '<div id="g-quiz" class="body" style="display:block"></div>', "This plays by itself. Each bar is our model's real probability. It gets 8 of 10 of this set right; the two it missed are not shown in the animation.", "Decision making: answering", "Our model <i>picks the answer</i>")
S("Start", "Choosing a tool", '<div id="g-tools" class="body" style="display:block"></div>', "This plays by itself. The tool descriptions are text the model never trained on. It gets 8 of 10 right; the two it missed are not shown in the animation.", "Decision making: agent tools", "Our model <i>picks the tool</i>")
S("Start", "Link race", '<div id="g-race" class="body" style="display:block"></div>', "This plays by itself. Our own small link graph, in the spirit of WikiRacing. Our pre-trained head wins 4 of 10 races; the animation shows the wins.", "Decision making: finding a path", "Our model <i>finds its way</i>")

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Idea
S("The idea", "Decision", '<div class="body" style="display:block">' + tbl([["Customer: &ldquo;I was charged twice&rdquo;", "billing, technical", "billing"], ["Two cacti ahead, 96 px away", "jump, duck, run", "jump"], ["Agent has just read an error log", "edit file, run tests, stop", "edit file"]], ["Situation", "Options", "Pick"]) + '<p class="lead" style="margin-top:44px">Agents make thousands of these. Most need a good choice made quickly, not an essay.</p></div>', "The options exist before the model runs.", "What is a decision?", "A situation, a list of options, <i>and one pick</i>")
S("The idea", "Generate vs choose", '''<div class="grid2" style="margin-top:44px"><div class="tile"><h3>A normal LLM writes</h3><p class="mono" style="font-size:30px;margin-top:24px">The &rarr; best &rarr; action &rarr; is &rarr; jump</p><p>One forward pass per output token. Then your code reads the text to find the choice.</p></div>
<div class="tile hot"><h3>A System One model scores</h3><p class="mono" style="font-size:30px;margin-top:24px">jump 0.97 &middot; duck 0.02 &middot; run 0.01</p><p>No output tokens. A probability for every option, directly.</p></div></div><p class="lead" style="margin-top:50px">The trade: it cannot invent an option you did not give it.</p><p class="note" style="margin-top:14px">The probabilities are an illustration.</p>''', "", "Generating versus choosing", "Why write when you can <i>choose</i>?")
S("The idea", "Fast and slow", """<div class="body" style="gap:50px;align-items:center"><div style="display:flex;gap:22px;flex:none;align-items:flex-end"><figure style="margin:0"><img src="img/kahneman.jpg" alt="Daniel Kahneman" style="width:330px;height:400px;object-fit:cover;display:block"><figcaption class="note" style="margin-top:8px;font-size:17px;color:#000">Daniel Kahneman, 1934 to 2024<br>Nobel Prize in Economics, 2002</figcaption></figure><figure style="margin:0"><img src="img/book.jpg" alt="Cover of Thinking, Fast and Slow by Daniel Kahneman" style="height:400px;width:auto;display:block;border:1px solid #dcdcdc"><figcaption class="note" style="margin-top:8px;font-size:17px;color:#000">Thinking, Fast and Slow<br>2011</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="col"><div class="grid2" style="gap:30px"><div class="tile hot"><div class="n">The fast mind</div><h3 style="font-size:60px;font-weight:300">System 1</h3><p>Automatic, quick and effortless.</p><p class="mono" style="font-size:42px;color:#4d6bfe">2 + 2 = ?</p></div><div class="tile"><div class="n">The slow mind</div><h3 style="font-size:60px;font-weight:300">System 2</h3><p>Deliberate, slow and effortful.</p><p class="mono" style="font-size:42px">17 &times; 24 = ?</p></div></div>
<div style="margin-top:38px"><table class="tbl" style="font-size:33px"><tr><td style="color:#4d6bfe">System One model</td><td>Sees the situation and answers in one quick pass</td></tr><tr><td>Normal LLM</td><td>Works it out token by token, one step at a time</td></tr></table></div></div></div><p class="note" style="margin-top:8px">The mapping to models is an analogy. Photo: nrkbeta, CC BY-SA 2.0, via Wikimedia Commons. Cover: Open Library.</p>""", "You answer 2 plus 2 without trying, and you have to stop and work out 17 times 24. Kahneman calls these System 1 and System 2. A System One model is built for the fast kind of decision. This is an analogy: the model is not a brain, and the fast mind also makes mistakes, which is why we test it.", "Where the name fits", "Your <i>fast mind</i> and your slow mind")
S("The idea", "Jev and CLM", '<div class="body" style="display:block">' + tbl([["Made by", "TypeSafe", "Stanford and NVIDIA Research"], ["Weights", "Not public", "Public, Apache 2.0"], ["Method", "Not public", "Blog post and serving code"], ["Training data", "Not public", "Q&amp;A vectors public"], ["Interface", "Typed questions", "The same request format"]], ["", "Jev", "CLM-8B"]) + '<p class="lead" style="margin-top:36px">We can call Jev, but we cannot see how it was built. So we rebuild CLM.</p></div>', "", "Jev is closed. CLM is open.", "An <i>open</i> System One model")
S("The idea", "Whole idea", '<div class="body c"><p style="font-size:82px;font-weight:300;line-height:1.14;letter-spacing:-.03em;max-width:1560px">Turn every state and every action into a vector. Train so a state lands close to the action that was taken. <span style="color:#4d6bfe"><i>At runtime, the closest action is the decision.</i></span></p></div>', "Everything after this is detail on three questions: how we make the vectors, how we train them, and what data teaches them.")

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Model
blk = lambda t, sub, bg="#f4f4f4", c="#000", b="none": f'<div style="background:{bg};color:{c};border:{b};padding:8px 20px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:24px"><span style="font-size:32px">{t}</span><span class="mono" style="font-size:22px;opacity:.75">{sub}</span></div>'
arrow = '<div class="mono" style="text-align:center;color:#8c8c8c;font-size:22px;line-height:1;margin:1px 0">&darr;</div>'
S("The model", "Qwen architecture", f'''<div class="body"><div class="col w3" style="flex:1.45">
{blk("Input tokens", "up to 2,048 here")}{arrow}
{blk("Token embedding", "151,936 &times; 4,096 &middot; 622.3M")}{arrow}
<div style="border:2px solid #000;padding:14px 18px 16px"><div class="mono" style="font-size:24px;margin-bottom:10px">36 identical decoder layers &middot; 192.9M each &middot; 6.95B total</div>
{blk("RMSNorm", "4,096")}{arrow}{blk("Self-attention with RoPE", "32 heads, 8 KV heads &middot; 41.9M")}{arrow}{blk("RMSNorm", "4,096")}{arrow}{blk("Feed-forward, SiLU", "4,096 &rarr; 12,288 &rarr; 4,096 &middot; 151.0M")}</div>{arrow}
{blk("Final RMSNorm", "4,096")}{arrow}
{blk("Linear output head", "4,096 &rarr; 151,936 &middot; 622.3M", "#fde8e6", "#b42318", "2px solid #b42318")}{arrow}
{blk("Next-token probabilities", "over 151,936 tokens", "#fde8e6", "#b42318")}
</div><div class="col"><div class="tile"><div class="n">Total</div><h3 style="font-size:64px;font-weight:300">8,190,735,360</h3><p>parameters, from the model&rsquo;s own files. The layer sizes add up to exactly this.</p></div>
<p class="lead" style="margin-top:40px">A normal Qwen writes text. The <span style="color:#b42318">red part</span> turns the last hidden state into next-token probabilities.</p><p class="note" style="margin-top:24px"><a href="https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-8B">Qwen/Qwen3-8B</a>. Head dimension 128, RoPE theta 1,000,000.</p></div></div>''', "Walk from the top. Count the layer parameters on the board: 41.9M attention plus 151.0M feed-forward plus norms gives 192.9M. Times 36, plus two 622.3M ends, gives 8.19B.", "Step 1: the model as it ships", "Qwen3-8B, <i>the full architecture</i>")
S("The model", "What we replace", f'''<div class="body"><div class="col"><div class="kick">Original Qwen</div>{blk("Tokens", "")}{arrow}{blk("Embedding + 36 layers + norm", "frozen", "#16213a", "#fff")}{arrow}{blk("Linear output head", "622.3M", "#fde8e6", "#b42318", "2px solid #b42318")}{arrow}{blk("Next-token probabilities", "", "#fde8e6", "#b42318")}</div>
<div class="col"><div class="kick" style="color:#4d6bfe">Our model</div>{blk("Tokens", "")}{arrow}{blk("Embedding + 36 layers + norm", "the same weights, frozen", "#16213a", "#fff")}{arrow}{blk("Hidden state of the last token", "4,096 numbers", "#eef1ff", "#000", "2px solid #4d6bfe")}{arrow}{blk("Normalize to length 1", "", "#eef1ff", "#000", "2px solid #4d6bfe")}{arrow}{blk("One small trained head", "9.44M", "#4d6bfe", "#fff")}{arrow}{blk("One vector", "512 numbers", "#4d6bfe", "#fff")}</div></div><p class="lead" style="margin-top:6px">Remove the output head. Freeze everything else. Add a small trained head.</p>''', "We never compute next-token probabilities. Qwen's weights never receive a gradient.", "Step 2: exactly what changes", "We replace <i>only the end</i>")
sh = lambda name, col: f'<div class="mono" style="font-size:26px;color:{col};margin-bottom:10px">{name}</div>' + tbl([["Linear 4,096 &rarr; 1,536, GELU", "6,292,992"], ["Linear 1,536 &rarr; 1,536", "2,360,832"], ["LayerNorm, GELU", "3,072"], ["Linear 1,536 &rarr; 512", "786,944"], ["<b>Total</b>", "<b>9,443,840</b>"]], size=30)
S("The model", "Two networks", f'''<div class="grid2" style="margin-top:30px"><div><div style="font-size:34px;margin-bottom:18px">Question + document &rarr; frozen Qwen &rarr;</div>{sh("STATE HEAD", "#4d6bfe")}</div><div><div style="font-size:34px;margin-bottom:18px">Answer &rarr; the same frozen Qwen &rarr;</div>{sh("ACTION HEAD", "#b42318")}</div></div>
<p class="lead" style="margin-top:34px">Same shape, separate weights. Score = cosine of the two 512-d vectors &times; a learned scale. Together: <b style="font-weight:500">18,887,680 trained parameters</b>.</p>''', "There are not two LLMs. There is one Qwen and two heads. They learn together from one loss, so their outputs land in one shared space.", "Step 3: the two networks", "Questions go through one, <i>answers through the other</i>")

