S("Data", "Hard negatives", '<div class="body" style="display:block">' + tbl([["How does p21 affect the viral polymerase complex?", "It perturbs it", "It enhances it &middot; It stabilizes it &middot; It inhibits it"], ["How long were the production runs?", "50 ns", "2 ns &middot; 50 ps &middot; 500 ns"], ["What type of data was collected every hour?", "Ambient PM2.5 levels", "Temperature and noise data &middot; Relative humidity data"], ["Which theory involves the coupling of states from different n?", "Wannier theory", "Rydberg formula &middot; Schrodinger equation"]], ["Question", "Correct", "Tricky wrong answers, from Gemini"], size=30) + '<p class="say" style="margin-top:30px">Up to 10 per question. The topic is identical, so only the exact meaning separates them.</p><p class="note" style="margin-top:10px">Real rows, shortened to fit the slide.</p></div>', "Real rows, with the longer answers shortened to fit. This is the difference between knowing the topic and knowing the answer.", "Real hard negatives", "Close wrong answers <i>are the point</i>")
S("Data", "Vectors", '''<div class="body" style="display:block"><p class="lead">Qwen runs over the data once. Training only ever reads the files.</p><pre class="mono" style="background:#f4f4f4;padding:30px;font-size:31px;line-height:1.55;margin-top:30px">shard_00/chunk_0000_q.npy     100,000 &times; 4,096, float16
shard_00/chunk_0000_a.npy     100,000 &times; 4,096, float16
shard_00/chunk_0000_meta      doc_id, pair_idx</pre><div class="grid3" style="margin-top:36px"><div class="tile"><h3>Aligned</h3><p>Row i of q matches row i of a</p></div><div class="tile"><h3>Size</h3><p>625 chunks, about 1 TB</p></div><div class="tile hot"><h3>Checked</h3><p>Our own embeddings match, cosine 0.9999+</p></div></div></div>''', "This is what makes the project affordable. Each pair costs 16 KB on disk.", "From text to saved vectors", "The encoder runs <i>only once</i>")

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Training
S("Training", "Watch it train", """<div class="body" style="margin-top:20px;gap:40px"><div class="col" style="flex:1.25"><div style="display:flex;gap:10px;margin-bottom:12px" id="tr-stages"></div><svg id="tr-chart" class="dia" viewBox="0 0 1000 470" role="img" aria-label="Tricky question accuracy during training"></svg><div class="grid4" style="gap:18px;margin-top:10px"><div class="tile"><div class="n">Step</div><div class="bignum" style="font-size:50px" id="tr-step">0</div></div><div class="tile"><div class="n">Pairs seen</div><div class="bignum" style="font-size:50px" id="tr-seen">0</div></div><div class="tile"><div class="n">General loss</div><div class="bignum" style="font-size:50px" id="tr-loss">6.93</div></div><div class="tile hot"><div class="n">Tricky test</div><div class="bignum" style="font-size:50px;color:#4d6bfe" id="tr-acc">8.0%</div></div></div></div>
<div class="col" style="flex:.75"><div class="kick" style="font-size:21px;margin-bottom:8px">8 real questions &times; their 8 answers</div><div id="tr-mat"></div><div class="mono" style="font-size:22px;margin-top:10px" id="tr-hits"></div><p style="margin-top:16px"><button id="tr-go">Replay training</button></p><p class="note" style="margin-top:12px;font-size:17px">Real logs, sped up. Real head outputs after each stage.</p></div></div>""", "This starts by itself. It is a replay of our real logs from today: 30,000 pre-training steps, then 1,008 mid-training steps, then 400 post-training steps. Watch the diagonal of the matrix form. The heads start from random numbers.", "Our real training run, replayed", "Watch it train <i>from random numbers</i>")
S("Training", "Batch", '''<div class="grid2" style="margin-top:44px"><div class="tile"><div class="n">Not this</div><h3 style="font-size:72px;font-weight:300">60M &times; 60M</h3><p>About 14 petabytes for one table.</p></div><div class="tile hot"><div class="n">This</div><h3 style="font-size:72px;font-weight:300">16,384 &times; 16,384</h3><p>About 1 GB, with a new random batch each step.</p></div></div><p class="lead" style="margin-top:50px">It is a match-the-columns exam. The other 16,383 answers in the batch are the wrong options, so nobody writes them by hand.</p>''', "Ask the room how big the full table would be before you show it.", "Pre-training", "A <i>match-the-columns</i> exam")
S("Training", "InfoNCE", '''<div class="body"><div class="col"><table class="tbl"><tr><th></th><th>Moon&rsquo;s gravity</th><th>Shakespeare</th></tr><tr><td>What causes tides?</td><td style="color:#4d6bfe"><b style="font-weight:500">0.30</b></td><td>0.25</td></tr><tr><td>Who wrote Romeo and Juliet?</td><td>0.10</td><td style="color:#4d6bfe"><b style="font-weight:500">0.30</b></td></tr></table><div class="mono" style="font-size:26px;margin-top:40px">Scale: <span id="sv">10</span></div><input id="scale" type="range" min="1" max="100" value="10" style="width:100%;accent-color:#4d6bfe;height:36px"><p class="note" style="margin-top:12px">Scores are made up for teaching. Our trained scale reached the cap of 100.</p></div><div class="col"><div class="kick">First row</div><div id="i1" style="font-size:36px;line-height:1.6;font-weight:300"></div><div class="tile hot" style="margin-top:30px"><div class="n">Loss, rows and columns averaged</div><div class="bignum" id="il"></div></div></div></div>''', "Drag the scale live. Each row is plain cross-entropy where the correct class is the diagonal. The loss is 0.30 at scale 10.", "The InfoNCE loss", "Put the probability <i>on the diagonal</i>")
S("Training", "Code", '''<pre class="mono" style="background:#f4f4f4;padding:34px;font-size:32px;line-height:1.55;margin-top:30px">s = F.normalize(state_head(q), dim=-1)
a = F.normalize(action_head(ans), dim=-1)

logits = scale * s @ a.T            <span style="color:#4d6bfe"># the table</span>
logits = hide_same_document(logits) <span style="color:#4d6bfe"># related answers are not wrong</span>
labels = torch.arange(len(s))       <span style="color:#4d6bfe"># the diagonal</span>

loss = (F.cross_entropy(logits, labels) + F.cross_entropy(logits.T, labels)) / 2</pre><p class="say" style="margin-top:26px">Sanity check: the first step should cost ln(batch size). At 16,384 that is 9.70, and our first step measured <b style="font-weight:500">9.7053</b>.</p>''', "The rest of the trainer is data loading. Our trainer is pipeline/train_heads.py in the repo.", "The whole loss", "Six lines <i>of code</i>")
S("Training", "Full recipe", '<div class="body" style="display:block">' + tbl([["Data", "62.45M pairs", "2.8M pairs + negatives", "822k agent steps + replay", "22,576 steps"], ["Batch", "16,384", "16,384", "16,384", "512"], ["Learning rate", "0.00653, constant", "0.001, constant", "0.0003, constant", "0.00115, one cycle"], ["Our steps", "<b style='font-weight:500'>30,000</b>", "<b style='font-weight:500'>1,008</b>", "<b style='font-weight:500'>400</b>", "up to 20 epochs"], ["Passes over data", "about 7.9", "about 5.9, to our best", "about 4.8 of agent data", "best at epoch 10"], ["Authors&rsquo; best", "step 28,035", "step 420", "not published", "epoch 15"], ["GPU and time", "1 L40S, about 2.3 hours", "1 L40S, about 41 minutes", "1 L40S, 8 minutes", "1 A10, 12 seconds"]], ["", "Pre-training", "Mid-training", "Post-training", "DeepSWE fine-tune"], size=29) + '<p class="note" style="margin-top:22px">All stages: AdamW, no weight decay, gradient clip 1.0, start temperature 0.07 and learned, same-document pairs masked. Pre and mid settings come from the authors&rsquo; checkpoints. Post-training is our reconstruction.</p></div>', "This is the recipe on one slide. The repo README has the exact commands.", "The complete training recipe", "Every stage, <i>every number</i>")
S("Training", "Pre curve", '<div class="body" style="display:block">' + curve(pre_hn, 0.6, 0.0, 0.517, "authors&rsquo; final head: 51.7%", 30000) + '<p class="note" style="margin-top:6px;text-align:center">Training steps. Tricky question test: pick the right answer out of up to 11, on 191,161 held-out pairs. Random guessing scores about 9%. Raw Qwen scores 14.3%.</p></div>', "These are the real measurements from our own run.", "Pre-training, our real run", "From random guessing <i>to 51.4%</i>")
S("Training", "Mid", '<div class="body"><div class="col w3" style="flex:1.5">' + curve(mid_hn, 0.75, 0.45, 0.692, "authors&rsquo; final head: 69.2%", 1008, w=1100, h=620) + '''</div><div class="col"><table class="tbl" style="font-size:30px"><tr><th>State &rarr;</th><th>Options</th></tr><tr><td>Own answer</td><td style="color:#4d6bfe">correct</td></tr><tr><td>Rest of batch</td><td>wrong &times; 16,383</td></tr><tr><td>Own tricky answers</td><td style="color:#b42318">wrong &times; 10</td></tr></table><p class="say" style="margin-top:30px">Extra columns in one direction only. Everything else stays the same.</p><p class="say" style="margin-top:24px">Starting with hard negatives from step 0 peaks lower: 62.4% in the blog.</p></div></div>''', "Mid-training gains the most for the least compute of any stage.", "Mid-training, our real run", "Same table, <i>tricky columns added</i>")
S("Training", "Agent", '''<div class="body"><div class="col" style="flex:.8"><img src="media/agent.png" alt="Illustration of a small robot choosing one lit path among many" style="width:100%;display:block"><p class="lead" style="font-size:32px">An agent is a model in a loop: see, decide, act, see the result.</p></div><div class="col" style="flex:1.2">''' + tbl([["Task + the room: a bed, a desk, a dresser", "<span class='mono' style='font-size:26px'>go to desk 1</span>"], ["All of that + what is on the desk", "<span class='mono' style='font-size:26px'>take alarmclock 1</span>"], ["All of that + &ldquo;You pick up the alarmclock&rdquo;", "<span class='mono' style='font-size:26px'>go to dresser 1</span>"]], ["State: everything seen so far", "Action: what it did next"], size=31) + '''<p class="say" style="margin-top:26px">One recording becomes many pairs. Sources: <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/neulab/adp-v2">Agent Data Protocol</a>, including LiteCoder-Terminal-SFT.</p><p class="note" style="margin-top:12px">Adapted from a real recording. The authors&rsquo; conversion is not public, so this is our reconstruction. The illustration is generated art.</p></div></div>''', "Same InfoNCE table. Question to answer becomes situation to next move.", "Post-training", "From question and answer <i>to next move</i>")
S("Training", "Replay", '<div class="body" style="display:block">' + bars([("Before post", 68.5, "#b9b9b9"), ("Hard-negative replay", 69.0, "#4d6bfe"), ("Plain Q&amp;A replay", 59.8, "#b42318")], 100, "%") + '<p class="lead" style="margin-top:34px">Each batch: 60% agent steps, 40% old Q&amp;A. Our finding: <b style="font-weight:500">the replay needs its hard negatives</b>, or the model forgets fine distinctions.</p><p class="note" style="margin-top:14px">Tricky question test, our runs at learning rate 0.0003. Blog: 69% before, 68.5% with replay, 56.2% with agent data only. The blog does not say what its replay contained, so this is our inference.</p></div>', "Like an internship: keep revising or forget the old exam.", "Keep revising, or forget", "Replay is <i>not optional</i>")

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Runtime
S("Runtime", "Runtime", '<div class="body" style="display:block">' + tbl([["0", "Before play: each action &rarr; Qwen &rarr; action head &rarr; cache", "Once per action text"], ["1", "Build the state: context, then question", "Nothing"], ["2", "New state &rarr; Qwen &rarr; state head", "<b style='font-weight:500'>The slow step</b>"], ["3", "Dot product with every cached action vector", "Almost free"], ["4", "Softmax, take the highest, act", "Almost free"]], ["", "One decision at step t", "Cost"]) + '<p class="lead" style="margin-top:34px">The training answers are gone. The cache holds <i style="color:#4d6bfe">your application&rsquo;s</i> actions, and they can be text it never saw. That is zero-shot.</p></div>', "Read from src/clm/engine.py and cache.py.", "Runtime", "What runs, and <i>what is cached</i>")
S("Runtime", "Cache", '<div class="body" style="display:block">' + bars([("4 actions, cached", 42.0, "#4d6bfe"), ("1,000, cached", 42.1, "#4d6bfe")], 150, " ms") + bars([("1,000, no cache", 6900, "#b42318")], 6900, " ms") + '<p class="lead" style="margin-top:30px">Going from 4 to 1,000 actions costs almost nothing. Without the cache it is about <b style="font-weight:500">160 times slower</b>.</p><p class="note" style="margin-top:14px">Our measurement, released head, A10 GPU, a new state every decision. The two charts use different scales. The cache key is the head version plus the exact text.</p></div>', "Scoring 1,000 cached actions took 0.26 ms. The encoder pass over the state takes the rest.", "What the cache buys", "1,000 options, <i>no extra cost</i>")

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Results
S("Results", "Scorecard", '<div class="body" style="display:block">' + tbl([["Tricky Q&amp;A, after pre-training", "52.1%", "<b style='font-weight:500;color:#4d6bfe'>51.4%</b>"], ["Tricky Q&amp;A, after mid-training", "69.2%", "<b style='font-weight:500;color:#4d6bfe'>68.5%</b>"], ["Tricky Q&amp;A, after post-training", "68.5%", "<b style='font-weight:500;color:#4d6bfe'>69.0%</b>"], ["DeepSWE, seed 1234", "31/38", "<b style='font-weight:500;color:#4d6bfe'>31/38</b>"], ["T-Rex answer time", "16.5 ms", "<b style='font-weight:500;color:#4d6bfe'>17.1 ms</b>"], ["T-Rex courses survived, shield on", "5/5", "<b style='font-weight:500;color:#b42318'>3/5</b>"]], ["Test", "Published", "Our model"]) + '<p class="say" style="margin-top:28px">Q&amp;A, verifier and speed replicate. The game&rsquo;s decision quality does not yet: planner agreement is 10%, against about 66%. Post-training is the stage whose recipe is not public.</p></div>', "This is the honest scorecard. The gap is the next research problem, and a good one to invite students to work on.", "Did we replicate it?", "Most of it, <i>and one clear gap</i>")
S("Results", "Faster than Jev", '<div class="body" style="display:block">' + bars([("Our model", 17.1, "#4d6bfe"), ("Jev", 149.8, "#b9b9b9")], 149.8, " ms") + '<p class="lead" style="margin-top:34px">About <b style="font-weight:500;color:#4d6bfe">8.8 times faster</b> on the dinosaur game.</p><p class="note" style="margin-top:14px">Median time per answer. Ours: our run on one L40S GPU. Jev: the authors&rsquo; logged run through TypeSafe&rsquo;s API, on a different setup. We did not run Jev ourselves.</p></div>', "Speed is the clear win.", "Where we beat Jev: speed", "Lower is <i>better</i>")
S("Results", "DeepSWE what", '<div class="body"><div class="col"><p class="say">A coding benchmark. An agent attempts real software tasks, and a test suite decides pass or fail.</p><div class="kick" style="margin-top:30px">Real held-out tasks</div><div class="mono" style="font-size:24px;line-height:1.55">fastapi-implicit-head-options<br>httpx-multipart-response-parsing<br>fd-deterministic-multi-key-sorting<br>dasel-html-document-format<br>bandit-structured-nosec-directives</div></div><div class="col"><table class="tbl" style="font-size:31px"><tr><th>The verifier&rsquo;s job</th></tr><tr><td>1. An agent attempts each task 4 times</td></tr><tr><td>2. Our model scores every step of every attempt</td></tr><tr><td>3. Average the last 12 step scores</td></tr><tr><td>4. Pick the attempt with the highest score</td></tr><tr><td>5. Did the picked attempt pass its tests?</td></tr></table><p class="note" style="margin-top:18px">38 held-out tasks, attempts by Claude Opus 5. Only 13 tasks are decidable: on the rest, every attempt passes or every attempt fails.</p></div></div>', "Fine-tuning takes about 12 seconds on a small GPU, so run it live if you like.", "What is DeepSWE?", "Pick the attempt <i>that actually works</i>")
S("Results", "Beats Jev DeepSWE", '<div class="body" style="display:block">' + bars([("Perfect picker", 89.5, "#dcdcdc"), ("Our model", 81.6, "#4d6bfe"), ("Random pick", 73.7, "#dcdcdc"), ("Jev", 71.1, "#b9b9b9")], 100, "%") + '<p class="say" style="margin-top:26px">Over 5 seeds we solved 31, 29, 30, 32 and 31 tasks, a mean of <b style="font-weight:500">30.6</b>. Random picking solves 28 and a perfect picker 34.</p><p class="note" style="margin-top:12px">Ours is seed 1234, our run. Jev&rsquo;s 71.1% is from the authors&rsquo; chart. One task is worth about 2.6 points.</p></div>', "Jev scores below random picking here, in the authors' chart.", "Where we beat Jev: verifier", "Ahead on <i>DeepSWE</i>")
S("Results", "All benchmarks", '<div class="body" style="display:block">' + tbl([["T-Rex game", "5/5", "5/5", "16.5", "149.8", "We ran it"], ["Tool calling, BFCL v4", "95.2%", "99.2%", "76.8", "125.5", "Harness not public"], ["WikiRacing", "26/30", "30/30", "79.8", "225", "Harness not public"], ["Super Mario", "5/5", "5/5", "33.5", "132.6", "Harness not public"], ["DeepSWE, fine-tuned", "81.6%", "71.1%", "79", "449", "We ran it"], ["Terminal-Bench 2.1, fine-tuned", "87.6%", "83.1%", "32", "131", "No public heads"]], ["The authors&rsquo; published numbers", "CLM", "Jev", "CLM ms", "Jev ms", "Rerun?"], size=30) + '<p class="say" style="margin-top:26px">CLM is faster everywhere and leads the verifier tests. Jev leads on tool calling and WikiRacing. Our Tool Picker and Link Race are our own smaller versions, because their harnesses are not public.</p></div>', "If asked for Mario or WikiRacing videos: their harnesses are not public, so we have no real runs to show.", "Every published benchmark", "The full picture")
S("Results", "What we learned", '<div class="body" style="display:block">' + tbl([["The recipe is inside the checkpoints", "Their stored settings reproduced the curve"], ["Replay needs hard negatives", "59.8% without them, 69.0% with them"], ["The README fine-tune misses", "Default data: 28/38. Their real 22,576 pairs: 31/38"], ["The seed matters", "It moved DeepSWE by up to 3 tasks"], ["The shield hides a lot", "Our model and theirs both survive 0 of 5 without it"]], ["We found", "The evidence"], size=33) + '<p class="lead" style="margin-top:30px">Read the checkpoint and the metadata. A blog and a README are only a summary of what really ran.</p></div>', "The DeepSWE reproduction matched their stored validation metric to every digit, 0.04514030093533957.", "What replicating taught us", "Measure <i>everything</i>")
S("Results", "Close", '''<div class="body c" style="flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:center"><h1 style="font-size:104px">Frozen encoder. Two small heads. <i>One simple loss.</i></h1><p class="lead" style="margin-top:44px">Code, training recipe, and results:</p><p class="mono" style="font-size:38px;margin-top:18px"><a href="https://github.com/shifanthottoli/system-one-model-clm">github.com/shifanthottoli/system-one-model-clm</a></p><p class="say" style="margin-top:50px">Explore the implementation, reproduce the evaluation, and help close the T-Rex gap.</p><p class="note" style="margin-top:20px">Maintained by Shifan T.</p></div>''', "Invite questions, and invite people to close the T-Rex gap.")

